{{smaller block|He tourneth all thynge ''topsy tervy''.
{{right|''Roy and Barlow'', Rede Me and Be Nott Wrothe (1528, [ed. Arber), p. 51.}}}}

{{smaller block|Now, beholde, all my enterprise bee quite pluckte backe, and my purposes tourned cleane ''topse-torve''.
{{right|''Barnaby Rich'', Farewell to Military Life (ed. 1846), p. 29.}}}}

{{smaller block|His trembling Tent all ''topsie turuie'' wheels.
{{right|''Sylvester'', tr. of Du Bartas's Weeks, ii., The Ark}}}}

{{smaller block|We shall o're-turne it ''topsie-turuy downe''.
{{right|''Shak.'', 1 Hen. IV. (fol. 1623), iv. 1.}}}}

{{smaller block|Here the winds not only blow together, but they turn the whole body of the ocean ''topsy-turvy''.
{{right|''Goldsmith'', Hyperbole.}}}}

